.TH SAPHIRA-EARLYFW 8 "October 2026" "Saphira" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
saphira-earlyfw \- build per-kernel early-firmware boot images
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B saphira-earlyfw --all
.RI [ --root " DIR"] " [" --boot " DIR"] [" --include " DIR"]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Built-in drivers initialize before the real root is mounted, so
.I /lib/firmware
on the root is not there yet. saphira-earlyfw packs the firmware
those drivers need into per-kernel
.I /boot/earlyfw-<release>.img
files (firmware only: no
.IR /init ,
no modules, no early userspace), plus
.I /boot/amd-ucode.img
when AMD blobs are installed. Intel microcode ships static in the
.B intel-ucode
package instead.
.PP
Selection is hardware-driven (PCI display controllers via sysfs
against the map, plus baseline includes for generic images); missing
firmware for present hardware fails loudly, and grub.cfg is
regenerated afterwards. Images whose kernel is gone are pruned.
.SH FILES
.I /usr/share/saphira/earlyfw/pci.map
.br
.I /etc/saphira/earlyfw.conf
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR saphira-mkinitramfs (8)
